    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Welcome to GkTeDPI</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">GkTeDPI combines two engines in one app:\n• Simple DPI Mode: 100%% on-device C packet desync with zero speed loss.\n• Real Country VPN: Encrypted multi-country tunnel (Netherlands, US, Germany &amp; more) that changes your public IP.\n\nBy continuing, you accept the Terms of Use &amp; Privacy Policy. Allowing unrestricted background battery usage is recommended so Android keeps your tunnel active.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_accept_btn">Accept &amp; Continue</string>

    <string name="about_screen_title">About &amp; Terms</string>
    <string name="about_full_desc_heading">About GkTeDPI</string>
    <string name="about_full_desc_body">GkTeDPI v6 is a dual-engine connectivity &amp; anti-DPI platform built with native C/JNI cores (byedpi + hev-socks5-tunnel), a multi-country encrypted VPN relay, and an optical Liquid Glass interface.\n\n• Real Multi-Country VPN: Connect to real encrypted servers in the Netherlands, USA, Germany, UK, France, Poland, Romania, Sweden, Finland, Canada, Japan, and Singapore with 0-RTT payload coalescing, encrypted DNS, and automatic fastest-node failover.\n• Simple Zero-Loss DPI Mode: Bypass ISP packet inspection 100%% locally on your phone with simplified 1-tap modes (Auto, Discord &amp; Voice, Gaming, Strong Access, Mobile Data) while preserving your full bandwidth and ping.</string>
    <string name="about_terms_heading">Terms of Use &amp; Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_terms_body">1. Zero-Log Policy &amp; Privacy: GkTeDPI does not log, store, or sell your browsing history or DNS queries.\n\n2. Dual-Engine Scope: In Simple DPI Mode, traffic stays local and your public IP does not change. In Real VPN Mode, traffic and DNS are encrypted and routed through your selected country\'s exit node (changing your public IP).\n\n3. Lawful Usage Responsibility: You are solely responsible for using GkTeDPI in compliance with applicable laws and network terms in your jurisdiction.\n\n4. Open-Source Components &amp; Disclaimer: Provided \"AS IS\" without warranty of any kind. Incorporates open-source native components under their respective licenses.</string>
